349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (The Electrical Systems team at Ashwa Racing has continued to make steady progress on the integration of both the High Voltage \(HV\) and Low Voltage \(LV\) systems on our vehicle. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (The work carried out this month primarily involved the completion of the temperature sensing and the cell tap harness routing within the segments in the HV sector. Mounting of the Low Voltage enclosure, harness and routing of the shutdown circuit and CAN communication lines was the progress along the LV sector. Each of these tasks contributes to the safe monitoring, control, and communication of critical electrical systems in the vehicle.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 166 0 R
/T (THE HIGH VOLTAGE SYSTEM )
/E (THE HIGH VOLTAGE SYSTEM )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 166 0 R
/E (The AMS \(Accumulator Management System\) registers temperature and battery voltage of the modules. Temperature monitoring plays a critical role in the safe operation of our 25R Samsung lithium-ion cells, which are the source of energy in the Accumulator. In case the operation temperature exceeds a given threshold, the car is immediately shut down and the AMS indicator lights up to represent the fault. This is necessary as cells experience significant electrical and thermal loads during operation.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
