363 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 168 0 R
/T (On the other hand, progress was also made on the Low Voltage system, beginning with the mounting of the LV enclosure. It was mounted accounting for the grounding. In this arrangement, the ground of the Power Distribution Board \(PDB\) is connected directly to the chassis through the bolt it is affixed to. This establishes the chassis as the common electrical reference point for the LV circuitry. Proper grounding is essential for maintaining electrical stability, minimizing noise in communication signals, and ensuring consistent operation of sensors and control electronics.)
/E (On the other hand, progress was also made on the Low Voltage system, beginning with the mounting of the LV enclosure. It was mounted accounting for the grounding. In this arrangement, the ground of the Power Distribution Board \(PDB\) is connected directly to the chassis through the bolt it is affixed to. This establishes the chassis as the common electrical reference point for the LV circuitry. Proper grounding is essential for maintaining electrical stability, minimizing noise in communication signals, and ensuring consistent operation of sensors and control electronics.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
