374 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 169 0 R
/T (To implement this, the required wire lengths between components were measured based on the finalized electrical layout of the vehicle. The routing was performed while accounting for the presence of a firewall separating the driver compartment from the accumulator enclosure, which acts as a protective barrier between the high-energy system and the driver. Where wires needed to pass through the firewall, grommets were used to ensure safe routing. A grommet is a protective ring, typically made of rubber or insulating material, that is inserted into openings where wires pass through structural panels. This design ensures ease of removing the accumulator from the vehicle without having concerns about the wiring. The grommet enables the harness to be divided into two parts- from the cockpit to the firewall and from the firewall to the HV/LV enclosures. Once they are disconnected, the accumulator can be separated from the rest of the vehicle. )
/E (To implement this, the required wire lengths between components were measured based on the finalized electrical layout of the vehicle. The routing was performed while accounting for the presence of a firewall separating the driver compartment from the accumulator enclosure, which acts as a protective barrier between the high-energy system and the driver. Where wires needed to pass through the firewall, grommets were used to ensure safe routing. A grommet is a protective ring, typically made of rubber or insulating material, that is inserted into openings where wires pass through structural panels. This design ensures ease of removing the accumulator from the vehicle without having concerns about the wiring. The grommet enables the harness to be divided into two parts- from the cockpit to the firewall and from the firewall to the HV/LV enclosures. Once they are disconnected, the accumulator can be separated from the rest of the vehicle. )
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
