/Title (Throughout the wiring process, ferrules were used at wire terminations to ensure proper numbering and identification of wires. In order to maintain uniformity, connectors and crimps were standardized across all electrical systems. Adopting such methods proved useful for any member to identify faults and repair them without requiring the presence of other members. These practices also improve organization within the car and have thus simplified troubleshooting, maintenance, and future integration work. As the team transitions their designs into reality, the systems of safety and communication are kept alive throughout the processes.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2262 0 R
/First 2270 0 R
/Last 2270 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 2271 0 R
>>
endobj
